// a bool literal is not a number. the neighbouring case matters as much: `return true;` from a
// `: bool` function has to stay legal - it reported "the boolean literal 'true' cannot be
// implicitly converted to the expected type 'bool'" until the expected type was compared to the
// literal's own type first (see tests_eco/functions/return_integer_widths.eco for the working one)

function not_a_number() : float64
{
    return true;
}

echo not_a_number();
